# Auto detect text files and normalise line endings. LF in the WORKING COPY too, for every text
# file: git has always stored LF, so this only decides what a checkout writes -- and with
# core.autocrlf=true on the Windows boxes a bare text=auto wrote CRLF, while the C# rules below
# used to say CRLF outright. The result was a worktree split 1720 CRLF / 355 LF across tools that
# each preserved whatever they found, a standing set of "modified" files with empty diffs, and a
# "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warning on every diff. Settled 2026-09-11: eol=lf everywhere,
# matching .editorconfig; nothing in the repo needs CRLF (no .bat/.cmd).
* text=auto eol=lf

# C# / .NET
*.cs text eol=lf
*.csproj text eol=lf
*.props text eol=lf
*.targets text eol=lf
*.sln text eol=lf
# Config / markup
*.json text eol=lf
*.xml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf
*.editorconfig text eol=lf
# Shell scripts — always LF
*.sh text eol=lf
# Shaders
*.glsl text eol=lf
*.vert text eol=lf
*.frag text eol=lf
*.comp text eol=lf
*.spv binary
# Binary — no conversion
*.png binary
*.fits binary
*.fit binary
*.fts binary
# fpack tile-compressed FITS. Auto-detection calls this one TEXT -- the compressed payload
# contains 0x0A bytes -- so without this, text=auto rewrites line endings inside a binary.
*.fz binary
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
*.nupkg binary
*.snk binary
*.pfx binary
*.gz binary
*.tgz binary
*.zip binary
*.lz binary
*.lzip binary
*.lz filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.fits.gz filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.bin.gz filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.bin.zip filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
tyc2.bin filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.ttf filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# In-house AI model weights (src/TianWen.AI.Imaging/models/) - small enough to
# live in the repo, too binary to diff. The fetch script materializes them into
# %LOCALAPPDATA%/TianWen/models; CI narrow-pulls them for the parity tests.
*.onnx filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# (2026-08-19 to 2026-09-06 this directory carried an `!filter !diff !merge` exemption from the rule
# above, because the LFS budget was exhausted and CI could not fetch a single new object. The budget
# is back, so the exemption is gone and these weights are LFS objects again. Two things the revert
# has to keep true, both wired: the publish matrix takes an ARTIFACT rather than pulling LFS, so a
# new object must be in `lfs-payload.list` or every released binary ships a pointer stub as its
# model file; and the 3.1 MB v19d blob stays in history either way, which is why nobody rewrote it.)

*.bz2 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.so filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# Canon raw fixtures - keep repo slim, narrow-pull in CI
*.cr2 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.cr3 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.CR2 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.CR3 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
